			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["398DA3318FB70483"]
			description: [
				"&7[NCP Field Memo #0102: Strata]"
				""
				"Hammer cobblestone into gravel and, now and then, the void gives something back: a &bStratum&r."
				"Strata are layers of the old world. Smelt one for a few nuggets (nine nuggets make an ingot); crush it later for a whole dust."
				"&7The stone hammer only finds iron and copper. Better hammers dig deeper: an iron-grade hammer finds tin, coal and lead"
				"&7in gravel; a steel hammer finds redstone and nickel in sand. After that, strata come from machines."
			]
			id: "CFDF70CCAFE922AC"
			rewards: [
				{
					count: 2
					id: "5468AE95DAD235D4"
					item: "positronics:ncp_scrip"
					type: "item"
				}
